  "notes": [
    "Set A resolved cleanly to 5 gate / 5 context: explicit conditional/rule statements (0001 'only once... should you take a trade', 0003 wait-for-retrace, 0005 US-session-only filter, 0007 'rule number one wait for close below', 0009 wait break+retest before short) vs pure narration/UI-nav/indicator-setup (0002 intro, 0004 'back to the euro dollar chart', 0006 'fix this thing', 0008 vague 'now go ahead and exit', 0010 removing/keeping bases).",
    "Adjudication principle used for example-anchored quotes: a clause that STATES a condition->action rule or requirement (even inside a worked example) = gate-strength; a clause that merely POINTS AT / confirms an instance ('as you can see here', 'we do have X', 'right over here') without articulating a rule = context. This split drove borderline calls like 0062/0064 (0062 'this means we're taking calls' = rule, gate; 0064 'as you can see here... over VWAP so we're good' = instance-pointing, context) and 0199/0206/0218 ('we do have a displacement/FVG/CISD' = example confirmation, context) vs 0193/0204 (states OB-formation requirement, gate).",
    "Hardest items were the ICT/CRT and VWAP sets (B09/B11/B13) where directional-bias reasoning blurs with gate logic: I gated sweep->direction rules (0089 'turtle soup of highs, that means we are now bearish', 0114 'took out the low, it wants to move to opposite end') but treated bare target/expectation narration (0121 U-shaped-to-HOD, 0122 'move to opposite end' with no condition) as context. VWAP-is-support lines (0167/0173/0179) I read as the refuted-strawman the educator critiques -> context.",
    "Genuinely underspecified: 0029 (truncated 'swing Traders... same initial pr[ice]... with the twist' — no determinable gate) = cannot-determine; that was the only cost-free abstention I used. Fragmentary retest/zone clauses (0096 'once the market returns to this level', 0108 'the lowest possible zone in a buying scenario') I gated because the discount/retest trigger is unambiguous despite the fragment.",
    "All five Afrikaans items (0012-0016, concept jlShztsY3oA, english_gloss null) held as HELD_TRANSLATION per the dual-anchor rule — no fabricated gloss.",
    "Effort economics: Set A + the terse imperative-rule targets (~1 read each, seconds). The example-heavy sets (B08 EMA, B11 CRT, B12 candlestick, B14 ORB) cost the most because each quote required deciding rule-vs-narration; roughly 40-50 items sat in that gray zone and consumed most of the adjudication time. Tally: 106 gate-strength, 109 context, 1 cannot-determine, 5 HELD_TRANSLATION (221 total).",
